post_install() {
    cat <<EOF
==========================================================================
  WARNING: SECURITY NOTICE & EXPERIMENTAL SOFTWARE
==========================================================================
  OpenClaw is powerful experimental AI software that executes code
  and interacts with external services.
 
  SECURITY RISKS:
  - Prompt Injection: AI models can be tricked into executing malicious commands.
  - Remote Execution: If exposed to the internet, secure it properly.
  - Data Privacy: Ensure you trust the models and plugins you use.

  IMPORTANT: You must select 'bun' as the package manager for installing skills.
 
  You can run OpenClaw inside a Bubblewrap sandbox for added security, 
  but this is not a guarantee of isolation. 

  PACMAN HOOK:
  A sample pacman hook to automatically restart OpenClaw user services on
  upgrade is available at:
  /usr/share/doc/@PKGNAME@/openclaw-restart.hook.sample
  To use it, copy it to /etc/pacman.d/hooks/.

  EXTERNAL CHANNEL PLUGINS (WhatsApp, etc.):
  WhatsApp is NOT bundled in the core package — it is installed per-user via
  ClawHub/npm (see docs: channels/whatsapp). After upgrading openclaw-git,
  outdated plugins can fail with ERR_PACKAGE_PATH_NOT_EXPORTED (plugin-sdk
  path renames). Refresh with:
    openclaw plugins update whatsapp
  # or reinstall matching host:
    openclaw plugins install clawhub:@openclaw/whatsapp --force
  Then restart the gateway (or rely on the pacman restart hook above).
 
  Please read further documentation and security warnings at:
  file:///usr/share/doc/@PKGNAME@/README-arch.md
  file:///usr/share/doc/@PKGNAME@/README.md
 
==========================================================================
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}
